quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  32,21,We will surely make them taste some of the minor punishment (of this world) before the greater punishment (of the Hereafter). Perhaps they may return (to the right path).
  32,22,"Who is a greater wrongdoer than the one who is reminded of his Lord’s signs and then turns away from them? Indeed, We shall take vengeance upon the guilty."
  32,23,And We certainly gave Musa (Moses) the Book. So be not in doubt regarding his meeting (with Him). And We made him a guide for the Children of Israel.
  32,24,"We raised leaders among them, guiding (the people) according to Our command when they patiently endured and firmly believed in Our revelations."
  32,25,Surely your Lord will decide between them on the Day of Resurrection about what they used to differ.
  32,26,"Does it not guide them: how many generations We have destroyed before them, amidst (the ruins of) whose dwellings they walk? There are indeed signs in it. Will they not then listen?"
  32,27,"Do they not see that We carry rainwater to the barren land and produce (various) crops through it, from which they and their cattle eat? Do they not observe?"
  32,28,And they say: ‘When is this victory (of yours coming) if you are truthful?’
  32,29,"Say: ‘On the Day of victory, faith will not benefit those who disbelieved (in this world), nor will they be given respite.’"
  32,30,"So turn away from them and wait, and they (too) are waiting."
